#Решение_Runtime_Substrate_WorkGraph<[
Базис:
  Work Graph уже разделил intent tree layout, serialization boundary, OS integration loop and FlatBuffers/GBC evaluation.
  Открытый риск — смешать canonical project truth with runtime queue, UI snapshot, binary cache or future native reader before MVP proves the need.
Вектор:
  Canonical store for MVP and migration target is .bvc intent tree: WorkItems, protocols, evidence summaries and memory records live as reviewable Step atoms with stable ids, links and trace labels.
  Compatibility projection is work/backlog.bvc during migration: current UI/runtime readers may keep parsing it, but it is an index/projection over canonical intent atoms rather than the long-term ownership location.
  Derived snapshots are deterministic JSON for UI, workers, tests and graph/RAG context; they are safe to delete and rebuild from .bvc sources.
  SQLite is optional runtime substrate for queue/index/locks/history/scheduling: task_index, run_queue, run_log, claim locks, retry windows and efficient polling may live there, but status, evidence and decisions must reconcile back to canonical .bvc.
  FlatBuffers/GBC is optional derived binary slice after explicit triggers: large snapshots, zero-copy reader need, native/Zig/Go consumer, GFS overlay or cross-process ABI pressure. It must not serialize the whole Step language or become a hidden canonical store.
  NoSQL is not an MVP goal. Revisit only for remote collaborative writes, offline/online sync, document-scale query volume, managed remote document API requirements or query/event scale beyond intent tree plus JSON/SQLite projections.
  Zig/native role is future reader/performance/R&D: useful for schema-stable slice readers, validators, GBC/GFS experiments or high-performance indexing, not for MVP source of truth or mandatory memory core.
Цель:
  Runtime substrate is chosen as boring canonical .bvc plus rebuildable projections, with databases and binary/native formats introduced only as measured execution aids.

Проверки:
  canonical store choice is explicit
  compatibility backlog role is explicit
  JSON, SQLite, FlatBuffers/GBC, NoSQL and Zig roles are separated
  migration and operations do not make cache/queue/binary artifacts authoritative

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: runtime-substrate-decision
  decision.status: accepted
  work.source: choose-runtime-substrate
  source.canonical: step-intent-tree
  compatibility.projection: work/backlog.bvc
  runtime.snapshot: workgraph.snapshot.v1-json
  sqlite.role: optional-runtime-projection
  gbc.role: optional-derived-binary-slice
  nosql.scope: non-goal-mvp
  zig.role: future-native-reader-rnd
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Канонический_Store_And_Backlog_Projection<[
Базис:
  Current compatibility readers still consume work/backlog.bvc, while intent tree layout already defines smaller canonical WorkItem files.
Вектор:
  New source-of-truth writes should target intent/**/*.work.bvc and related .bvc protocol/evidence/memory atoms first.
  work/backlog.bvc remains a stable, reviewable projection for current parseWorkItems/buildSnapshot readers, queue ordering and migration compatibility.
  During transition, dual updates are allowed only to keep the mirror consistent; after reader cutover, backlog should be regenerated or checked from intent tree.
  Projection drift must be treated as verification failure: duplicate work.id, missing dependency, stale status or missing evidence should block trace.status verified.
Цель:
  Operators keep a familiar backlog surface while storage ownership moves to intent tree atoms.

Метки:
  atom.profile: trace
  contract.id: runtime-canonical-store-and-backlog-projection
  decision.id: runtime-substrate-decision
  trace.status: verified
]>

#JSON_SQLite_And_Runtime_Operations<[
Базис:
  UI, workers and schedulers need fast read models, but read speed is not the same as project truth.
Вектор:
  JSON snapshots remain the first interchange for operator dashboard, worker input, tests, derived graph and RAG context because browsers and tools consume them directly and diffs stay readable.
  SQLite may be introduced when runtime needs durable claims, multi-process locking, scheduled runs, retry/rate-limit state, crash recovery, history, action feed joins or efficient polling.
  SQLite tables must be projection-oriented and rebuildable from .bvc plus worker/evidence outputs; writes that affect WorkItem state become transition proposals and evidence records, not silent DB mutations.
  Runtime startup should tolerate missing SQLite by rebuilding from .bvc/JSON; corruption or stale SQLite should be recoverable by deleting the DB and replaying canonical atoms/log projections.
Цель:
  Local execution can become reliable without letting queue mechanics own task semantics.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: json-sqlite-runtime-roles
  decision.parent: runtime-substrate-decision
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Binary_Native_And_NoSQL_Boundaries<[
Базис:
  FlatBuffers/GBC, GFS, Zig/native readers and NoSQL can all be useful later, but each solves a different pressure.
Вектор:
  FlatBuffers/GBC starts only from an explicit derived-slice trigger and should cover a minimal WorkGraphSlice, WorkItem, DependencyEdge, EvidenceRef and SchemaVersion shape.
  Zig/native work is R&D or performance implementation for readers, validators, slice generation or indexing; it must read canonical/projection contracts rather than redefine Work Graph truth.
  NoSQL remains out of MVP because .bvc plus deterministic JSON plus optional SQLite covers current authoring, review, UI and local scheduling needs with less operational surface.
  Any future move toward NoSQL or binary-first canonical storage requires a separate architecture decision that preserves reviewability, stable ids, migration path, conflict handling and evidence gates.
Цель:
  Advanced substrate work stays available without becoming accidental architecture.

Метки:
  atom.profile: architecture_decision
  decision.id: binary-native-nosql-boundaries
  decision.parent: runtime-substrate-decision
  deferred.next_work: defer-gbc-gvm-zig-scope
  trace.status: verified
]>

#Migration_And_Operational_Implications<[
Базис:
  The project is already between backlog monolith compatibility and intent tree canonical layout.
Вектор:
  Migration should keep status/evidence edits synchronized between canonical intent task files and work/backlog.bvc until runtime readers scan intent roots directly.
  Tests must continue to compare snapshots across backlog projection and intent tree files, because runtime substrate errors usually appear as missing ids, stale statuses or broken dependency/evidence links.
  Operational commands should publish or serve JSON snapshots from canonical state; worker queues may cache runnable tasks but must re-check dependency/status gates before claim and before done.
  Backup/rollback is simple by design: .bvc atoms are reviewable in git, JSON/SQLite/GBC artifacts can be regenerated, and failed cache migrations should not require recovering hidden project state.
  Next architecture follow-up is to finalize GBC/GVM/Zig deferral scope so the team knows which native/binary experiments are outside MVP and which triggers bring them back.
Цель:
  Runtime substrate decision can guide implementation without forcing a database migration or binary runtime before the first operator/dashboard/golden-path loops are stable.

Метки:
  atom.profile: plan
  plan.id: runtime-substrate-migration-operations
  decision.id: runtime-substrate-decision
